{
 "about": "Design §8's rule for a directory's project (docs/doperpowers/specs/2026-11-10-project-registry-design.md), and §D's anchor comparison, hand-written from the design's text: the contract between sminos and MAWS (Interfaces §B of docs/doperpowers/plans/2026-11-10-project-registry.md, whose sync rule alone changes it). A harness makes each case's tree in a fresh directory, in `under` spelled as written when the case names one, every P relative to it; it hands its implementation each statement at the canonical form of its path (the real path, NFC), anchored to the folder there, but for `replaced`, whose anchor is another folder's, and `removed`, a removed row's; it asks each `dir` spelled as written, and expects `project`, `by` and `at`, the deciding folder's canonical path relative to the case's directory.",
